comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-01T12:13:39.832Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: exact all-status searches found general handled-error classifier fixes and snapshot primitives but no PM-CLI-2Q owner. Evidence stores only the public error class and release; raw events and private environment data remain outside PM."
  "2026-08-07T19:54:22.757Z","harness:codex","Live structured gate refresh 2026-08-07: PM-CLI-2Q remains one of two high groups in the 14-day release window after the gate moved from prose patterns to SDK error-code and exit-code classification. Telemetry is healthy at 0.91% finish errors with zero failures missing codes. This item remains open and unclaimed; only contract-level classification evidence is retained."
  "2026-08-08T07:58:25.530Z","harness:claude-code","Verified already fixed in HEAD rather than re-fixed. At v2026.7.29 validateSnapshotTarget threw a bare Error, which shouldCaptureCliError treats as unexpected and captures; commit acbd3f639 made it a PmCliError with code invalid_workspace_snapshot_target and EXIT_CODE.USAGE, and shouldCaptureCliError returns false for every PmCliError, so the refusal no longer reaches Sentry. Confirmed by diffing git show v2026.7.29:src/sdk/workspace-snapshot.ts against HEAD. Strengthened the existing name-validation test from a message-substring assertion to the actual contract (PmCliError instance, declared code, exit 2), so a regression to a bare throw fails the suite instead of silently reopening the release-blocking behaviour."
